  "source": "Ingredients: hollow-orbit js/game/items.js, Rust's where it has the item (spears, bow, arrows); the bed's rope is fibre here. Scrap is left out of the workbenches until it has a source (G7). Times are ours, between hollow-orbit's and Rust's. Every recipe is known from the start until the tech tree (G7). G4: gunpowder (30 charcoal and 20 sulphur make 10), pistol and rifle rounds (10 metal fragments and 5 gunpowder make 4 and 3, at workbench 1 and 2) and the rifle's tier (workbench 3) are hollow-orbit's and Rust's; Rust's gun parts (pipes, springs, tech trash) come from loot (G7), so until then the guns and attachments cost refined metal instead; the variants, attachments and the metal mask are ours. Building items (G3): hollow-orbit's plan, hammer, claim device (its tool cupboard), wooden and sheet metal doors and code lock; Rust's key lock, double and garage doors and workbench levels; gears and sheet metal aren't in the game yet, so the armoured door's are metal fragments. G5: Rust's raiding recipes and workbench levels (explosives 50 gunpowder, 3 low-grade fuel, 10 sulphur and 10 metal fragments at workbench 2; the timed charge 20 explosives at 3; the satchel-like bag charge four grenades at 1; the grenade 60 gunpowder and 20 metal fragments; rockets 10 explosives and 150 gunpowder, the high-velocity one 100 gunpowder; explosive rounds 20 gunpowder and 10 sulphur for two, at 3), so a timed charge costs 2,200 sulphur, a rocket 1,400, a bag charge 480 and an explosive round 25, as in Rust. Lamp oil stands in for low-grade fuel, fibre for cloth, rope and the stash, refined metal for tech trash and pipes. G7 animals: Rust's low-grade fuel recipe (3 animal fat and 1 cloth make 4 in 5 s) as a second way to make lamp oil, with its own key and id (179), beside the charcoal recipe; Rust's bone knife (30 bone fragments) and a bone club (20).",
